            <ArticleTitle>Spinal and radicular pain in pseudotumor cerebri.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>106-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 4 1/2-year-old girl presented with cervical spine and radicular pain with hypoactive biceps and brachioradialis stretch reflexes. A diagnosis of pseudotumor cerebri was made. The patient's symptoms resolved following the reduction of the elevated intracranial pressure. Abnormalities of the cervical spine and spinal cord were not detected. A mechanism to explain this &quot;false localizing&quot; sign is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
